      "message": "Hi @spinler@us.ibm.com,\n\nThank you for catching that issue.\n\nI\u0027ve addressed both concerns in Patch Set 8:\n\n1. **PowerButtonProfile support**: Restored the profile factory check. Now the code \n   properly delegates to custom profiles when available, and only uses the dynamic \n   discovery fallback when no profile exists.\n\n2. **Unused variable**: The `buttonMode` variable was intended to provide runtime \n   visibility into which mode (host select button vs. multi-power button) the system \n   is using. However, since it\u0027s not strictly necessary, I\u0027ve removed it to reduce \n   code clutter.\n\nThe core logic now works as follows:\n- Check if HostSelector exists and whether it\u0027s virtual\n- Set `hostSelectButtonMode` accordingly\n- Register power button handlers (via profile if available, otherwise fallback)\n\nPlease review Patch Set 8 and let me know if you have any additional feedback.\n\nThank you very much!",
